<title>USA: Integral Systems on road to stock split.</title>
<headline>Integral Systems on road to stock split.</headline>
<dateline>LANHAM, Md. 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integral Systems Inc said Thursday its board endorsed an increase in the number of authorized shares as a preliminary step to a &quot;significant stock split.&quot;</p>
<p>The company said in a release that if approved, the number of authorized shares will be increased to 10 million from 2 million.</p>
<p>The recommendations will be voted on at the annual shareholders meeting on March 6, 1997, Integral said.</p>
